The final gauge pressure is 11\text{ atm}, which corresponds to an absolute pressure of:
P_2 = P_{\text{gauge}} + P_{\text{atm}} = 11 + 1 = 12\text{ atm} = 12 \times 1.01 \times 10^5\text{ N m}^{-2}
The remaining moles of oxygen in the cylinder are:
n_2 = \frac{P_2 V}{R T} = \frac{(12 \times 1.01 \times 10^5) \times 0.03}{\left(\frac{100}{12}\right) \times 300} = \frac{36360}{2500} = 14.544\text{ moles}
The number of moles of oxygen withdrawn is:
