R T = 0.0831 \times 1000 = 83.1\text{ L atm mol}^{-1}
Calculating K_p:
K_p = \left(\frac{1}{2500}\right) \times 83.1 = \frac{83.1}{2500} = 0.03324 \approx 0.033

Therefore, K_p for the reaction at 1000 K is 0.033.
